{#snippet hero()}

> The *automatic* color scheme generator

{/snippet}

{#snippet intro()}

Color Horse is an automatic color scheme generator. Input two colors, and Color Horse will generate a pallette of 80 compatible colors as named CSS variables.

{/snippet}

{#snippet how()}

## How it works

Color Horse uses color theory to generate a harmonious color scheme from two input colors. It accomplishes this task by converting your colors to a modern color-space called "OKLCH."

In OKLCH, Color Horse extracts three components from each of your colors: hue, lightness, and saturation. Each hue is a number between 0 and 360, which can sit on a circle. By placing the two hues on a circle, Color Horse can then smoothly place another ten points on the circle to create the basis for a palette. Rather than attempting to place the points evenly, which would be impossible, Color Horse uses trigonometry to smoothly distribute available space to allow gentle spreading and clustering.

Try dragging the sliders to see how the hues in your color scheme shift:

{/snippet}

{#snippet palette()}

## Palette

To create your palette, choose a primary and secondary brand color. Drag the sliders to adjust your palette's lightness and saturation.

{/snippet}

